\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {One landscape, two regimes.} Both panels place the system on the same Gaussian free-energy bowl (grey contours; the black dot marks the mode, where free energy is least). \textbf  {(a) Equilibrium:} the flow is pure gradient descent on free energy, \(f=-\nabla F\) (blue arrows). Detailed balance holds, so trajectories fall to the mode and come to rest with no net probability current. \textbf  {(b) Far-from-equilibrium (NESS):} an antisymmetric \emph  {solenoidal} operator \(Q\) adds a conservative current, \(f=(Q-\mitGamma )\nabla F\) (orange streamlines), that flows along the level sets of \(F\). Free energy is still minimized, but probability mass circulates without end --- the hallmark of living, self-organizing systems. The Free Energy Principle is the descent term; Bayesian mechanics adds the circulation. Internal states \(\mitmu \) infer external states \(\miteta \) across a Markov blanket (sensory \(s\), active \(a\)). Figure rendered deterministically by \breaktt {scripts/generate\_overview\_figure.py} over the tested flow in \breaktt {src/free\_energy\_flow.py}.}}{3}{figure.caption.2}\protected@file@percent }
\providecommand*\caption@xref[2]{\@setref\relax\@undefined{#1}}
\newlabel{fig:overview}{{1}{3}{\textbf {One landscape, two regimes.} Both panels place the system on the same Gaussian free-energy bowl (grey contours; the black dot marks the mode, where free energy is least). \textbf {(a) Equilibrium:} the flow is pure gradient descent on free energy, \(f=-\nabla F\) (blue arrows). Detailed balance holds, so trajectories fall to the mode and come to rest with no net probability current. \textbf {(b) Far-from-equilibrium (NESS):} an antisymmetric \emph {solenoidal} operator \(Q\) adds a conservative current, \(f=(Q-\Gamma )\nabla F\) (orange streamlines), that flows along the level sets of \(F\). Free energy is still minimized, but probability mass circulates without end --- the hallmark of living, self-organizing systems. The Free Energy Principle is the descent term; Bayesian mechanics adds the circulation. Internal states \(\mu \) infer external states \(\eta \) across a Markov blanket (sensory \(s\), active \(a\)). Figure rendered deterministically by \protect \breaktt {scripts/generate\_overview\_figure.py} over the tested flow in \protect \breaktt {src/free\_energy\_flow.py}}{figure.caption.2}{}}
\newlabel{fig:overview@cref}{{[figure][1][]1}{[1][3][]3}{}{}{}}
